lipse. The schools and my boss were both yelling at me, both saying the eclipse wasn't a good enough excuse. I'm sorry, but it definitely was. I am so glad I did that. I would do it again in a heartbeat.replyalnwlsn 5 minutes ago | parent | next [–] Both myself and my boss took off work to see the last one. Though unplanned it was not, as eclipses can be predicted centuries in advance. I knew I would see it before even working there.replyUncle_Brumpus 19 minutes ago | parent | prev [–] I drove ~3 hours to the Vermont-Canada border... and then drove 14 hours home. I'd also do it again in a heartbeat.I almost signed up for a live-work program for a big music festival happening in Iceland, but the flights (the only thing not covered) were astronomically expensive and I had already made plans with my dad last weekend, and he's getting older so I really didn't want to bail on him.I would love to sit atop the Rock of Gibraltar (with 47,000 other people) for the next one, Aug 2 2027, but that is likely also a pipe-dream, because NORMAL flights to Gibraltar are already too expensive for me.reply Guidelines | FAQ | Lists | API | Security | Legal | Apply to YC | Contact Search:\n=== END PAGE TEXT ===\n\nGoal: Survey the top 3 Hacker News stories:\n\n1. From the front page, identify the FIRST 3 stories (ranked by score)\n2. For each story, drill into its comments thread\n3. Record in working memory for each story (story 1, 2, 3):\n   - story<N>_title (key=story1_title, story2_title, story3_title): the post title\n   - story<N>_top_comment (key=story1_top_comment, story2_top_comment, story3_top_comment): first 2 sentences of the top comment\n4. Call verify_completion for the goal_complete criterion after all 6 facts are recorded\n5. Call terminate(finalAnswer=...) with a 3-paragraph summary covering each story's title and a brief excerpt from its top comment.",
